From 66c6467cc8669814dc9e61724bc557c473ea886a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Walters <jackwalterswork@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:09:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] markdown: Shrink a picture to its column in a table
 that fits its container

A table told to fit its container gives each column a share of the
width, but no less than the least width of its content, and a picture's
least width is its whole width in pixels. One screenshot in a cell made
its column that wide and pushed the table off the side, while the same
picture in a paragraph shrank in proportion.

In such a table the picture's wrapper now starts from no width and grows
into its column, so the picture inside shrinks to the column and keeps
its proportions. The wrapper then fills the cell, so it places a small
picture by the column's alignment as the cell did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
